    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 4-layer spectrally selective absorber stack on aluminum substrate. Layer sequence from air side: SiO2 (variable thickness, bounds 50-150 nm), Cr (fixed thickness 32.0 nm, not optimized), HfO2 (variable thickness, bounds 216-254 nm centered on 235.05 nm with ±8% perturbation), SiO2 (variable thickness, bounds 137-161 nm centered on 148.74 nm with ±8% perturbation). Substrate: Aluminum (opaque). Illumination: normal incidence, unpolarized. Wavelength bands: 400-700 nm target high absorptance (low reflectance), 700-2000 nm target high reflectance. Objective: maximize weighted combination of mean absorptance in 400-700 nm and mean reflectance in 700-2000 nm. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with 500 iterations. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
